      "message": "Use the same type for `cd-service-id` in both lists\n\nThis list keys `cd-service-id` as string, but the `cd-services` list from `cross-domain-service-attributes` keys the same id as `uint8`, and `PceGraph` fills it with `Uint8.valueOf(...)`.\n\nAs it stands, the two ids have different Java types (`String` vs `Uint8`), so matching a path description to its cd-service needs a string-to-number conversion, and the type allows values that aren\u0027t a `cd-service-id` at all.\n\nI suggest using `uint8` here too, so `getCdServiceId()` returns `Uint8` on both sides and the join is just `cdServices.get(new CdServicesKey(pd.getCdServiceId()))`.\n\n```\nlist cd-service-path-description {\n  key \"cd-service-id\";\n  leaf cd-service-id {\n    type uint8;\n    description\n      \"Identifier of the cd-service this path applies to. Matches\n       cd-service-id in ../../../cross-domain-service/cd-services.\";\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nIf you want the schema to state the relationship, use a leafref instead. It generates the same Uint8 Java type:\n\n```\n  leaf cd-service-id {\n    type leafref {\n      path \"../../../cross-domain-service/cd-services/cd-service-id\";\n    }\n  }\n```\n\nPlain `uint8` is enough to fix the mismatch. The leafref additionally documents and constrains the reference in the schema.",
