      "message": "Keep the cross-domain data out of the per-service entries\n\nThis uses brings in the whole `path-description` grouping, including the `cross-domain` leaf and the `cross-domain-service` container. The `aggregated-path-description` description says those must not be filled here, but nothing in the model enforces that. A producer that copies a complete PathDescription into each entry puts the cross-domain data into the notification N+1 times, and the copies can disagree with the top-level `cross-domain-service` container.\n\nSuggestion: in transportpce-pathDescription@2026-04-22.yang, move the two direction containers into a grouping of their own and have `path-description` use it. PathDescription keeps the same children, so existing callers and generated code don\u0027t change.\n\n```\ngrouping path-directions {\n  description\n    \"A-to-Z and Z-to-A hop lists of a path, without cross-domain data.\";\n  container aToZ-direction { ... }   // moved unchanged\n  container zToA-direction { ... }   // moved unchanged\n}\n\ngrouping path-description {\n  description \"...\";\n  leaf cross-domain { ... }\n  container cross-domain-service { ... }\n  uses path-directions;\n}\n````\n\nThen here:\n\n```\nlist cd-service-path-description {\n  key \"cd-service-id\";\n  leaf cd-service-id { ... }\n  uses transportpce-pathDescription:path-directions;\n}\n```\n\nThe \"not supposed to be filled\" sentence in the aggregated-path-description description can then go, since the schema enforces it. Also mention the new grouping in the 2026-04-22 revision description.",
